3.9.m:
The wise man should have Brahmā made: gentle, four-faced, / seated in the lotus posture, pleasing, and clad in a black-antelope skin;
wearing matted locks, four-armed, standing in a chariot with seven swans; / one pair of his arms should rest in the palm of his left hand;
in one right hand, an auspicious rosary, / and a water-pot in the second; wearing all ornaments;
endowed with all auspicious marks, of peaceful form, O king; / lustrous as the tip of a lotus petal, with eyes closed in meditation.
One should fashion the god in an idol, or in a painting, or in modeling. / And one should make Viṣṇu, the god of gods, seated on Garuḍa.
